08:16:43.048 | Old road nearing plains. (road)
08:16:43.048 | The rumble of burdened caravan wheels carries across the area. Nature's fecundity floods the surrounds with the clamour of life in a chittering refrain. The stars glimmer down, broken only upon occasion by thin wisps of clouds. A rock-lined road meets a dirt track here, transitioning as it reaches farther in the wilderness of Sapience. The forest has faded away, the green ferns and bushes giving way to the unadulterated grasses of the plains. The flatter landscape of this Savannah starkly showcases a distant boulder, marring the rolling horizon with its looming shape. The nearby dwelling seems similarly out of place, a lone fortress of civilisation that has already fallen victim to decay. Long and double-storied, it seems to have once been worthy of the label mansion, but faded paint, broken windows, and a battered door reduce its splendour. Fresh new ruts are pressed deeply into the ground here. Turgid and blistered, a severed leg lies motionless here. A large cart rests here, stacked high with assorted containers secured with thick rope. There are 2 black-crowned nycticoraxes here. Slave Morasla, Pestilent Disciple is here, hidden. Her features are obscured by a darkened mask dripping with gold. She wields Adchachel's lament in her right hand. Steward Layta Lichlord, Red Reaper is here, hidden. Her features are obscured by an unsettling porcelain doll-face mask. She wields Agith'maal's ire in her left hand and a bone shield reinforced with blackened steel in her right. Truthseeker Vasyly is here. He wields Reaver, a dark brass morningstar in his left hand and Sentinel, a darkened-silver morningstar in his right. Eradicator Maldrantus is here, hidden. His features are obscured by a mask of lifevision. He wields a Shield of Absorption in his left hand and Agith'maal's ire in his right. Valkyri, Seeker of Elocution is here. She wields a Braincrusher flail in each hand. Wreathed in torrid fury, the Elemental Lord Agathon blazes bright. He wields a Shield of Absorption in his left hand. Tomekeeper Harkon d'Ivoire, Scourge of His Legion is here. He wields a leaf-bladed ritual knife in his left hand.
