08:28:39.740 | The rumble of burdened caravan wheels carries across the area. A noxious, red-hued fog overwhelms the area with a thick, palpable vapour. Dawn breaks across the land, the sky and its sparse clouds lit in fiery hues by the rising sun. Summoned to Mhaldor by the ritualistic skill of the Apostates, this bridge is little more than the skeletal remains of a gigantic leviathan slaughtered by the denizens of Mhaldor. The fleshy remains of the corpse have been long since devoured by the large birds of carrion that perch and circle eternally here. A long spine and giant ribcage are all that remain of this once-deadly beast that spans the deep Gruu'n chasm. Staring about himself with an eternal frown, a spectral gorilla broods here. Gavai, the Jamala is here, shrouded. His features are obscured by Revelation's Guise. He wields a timeworn serpent's dirk in his left hand and a Shield of Absorption in his right. Steward Layta Lichlord, Red Reaper is here, hidden. Her features are obscured by an unsettling porcelain doll-face mask. She wields Agith'maal's ire in her left hand and a bone shield reinforced with blackened steel in her right. Tyndran Tabethys Aristata, Tyrannical Butcher of Baelgrim is riding on a silvery spectral gorilla. She wields an exquisite Mhaldorian staff of sterling silver in her left hand and a Shield of Absorption in her right.
